  "date": "October 2026",
  "abstract": "Covers DNS-AID (DNS for AI Discovery), draft-mozleywilliams-dnsop-dnsaid-02: publishing AI agents as SVCB RRsets at their primary owner names, one record per agent protocol, AliasMode for _agents and DNS-SD names, the _index._agents organization index, DANE TLSA, DNSSEC, mandatory= downgrade rules, the proposed cap, cap-sha256, bap, policy, realm and well-known SvcParamKeys as private-use keys, and the consumer rules for discovery, trust, integrity and privacy. It lists two version lines: draft-mozleywilliams-dnsop-dnsaid-02 (current, posture name) and draft-mozleywilliams-dnsop-dnsaid-01 (legacy, with -00, upgraded from). SKILL.md holds the invariants and workflow; references split out versions, publishing records, and discovery.",
